  "root_causes": {
    "B32": "Wall-clock deadlines can expire before admission under host load; sleeps do not establish queue admission, and Close with a canceled wait context can return before asynchronous cancellation reaches the held operation.",
    "B33": "callback.Invoke contains panic but not Goexit. Goexit unwinds sync.Once and publishes Ready without assigning Err, so later scope expansion treats an empty result as successful."
  },
  "changes": {
    "B32": "Existing testing/synctest convention provides blocked-goroutine barriers and a scheduler-independent clock. Callback channels retain ownership until release; barriers establish queued callers and drain shutdown cancellation. Existing ownership, overload and admission assertions remain.",
    "B33": "Use the existing callback.Isolated helper so the Once owner receives a safe error after callback exit and caches that failure. global_scope.go exactly matches goway-data-layer; internal/callback already matched and is unchanged."
  },
  "branch_global_scope_identical": true,
  "branch_callback_identical": true,
